+## Switch IOP directory bounds (M02, 2026-11-09)
+
+[gta-recomp] `ps2xIOP/src/emulator/imports/iop_cdvd.cpp` now uses checked layout
+helpers in `include/ps2x/iop/detail/cdvd_directory.h`. The original directory
+sector-to-byte multiplication was uint32: a 4 GiB rounded directory wrapped
+to a 2048-byte allocation, while record appends had no capacity guard. A
+synthetic size-list plus the actual old writer reproduces a heap overrun under
+AddressSanitizer; no disc or large filesystem tree is required.
+
+Directory sizing now rejects unrepresentable padded metadata with wide checked
+arithmetic. Record append checks remaining capacity before pointer arithmetic
+and the shared writer checks it again. Failures propagate from self/parent/child
+records and the volume descriptor. Record identifiers must fit their encoded
+length; file sizes and aggregate sector advances reject overflow instead of
+truncating or wrapping. The original filename normalization/order and valid
+record bytes, padding, sector numbering and metadata layout remain unchanged.
+
+Public port regression tests call these same production helpers, including the
+4 GiB boundary without a large allocation. The root M02 report retains failing
+ASan output, old/new valid-record comparison, normal IOP suites and ARM warning
+checks; target execution remains separately required. No warning is suppressed.
